      en: "The Gârbovăț Forest Reserve is located in the Anenii Noi District of eastern Moldova and serves as a vital protected area for the country's original forest-steppe vegetation. Spanning over 1,000 hectares, the reserve primarily consists of pubescent oak and pedunculate oak forests. Geographically, it is situated on a plateau that slopes gently toward the Dniester River valley. The flora is particularly precious, featuring rare herbs and shrubs typical of the Pontic steppe zone. The reserve supports a variety of wildlife, including foxes, badgers, and a significant population of partridges. A distinctive feature is the pheasant hatchery located within the forest, which contributes to the reintroduction of these birds across Moldova. The forest acts as an important recreational zone and a research center for forestry and nature conservation. Trails through the woods offer views of an ecosystem that has become increasingly rare due to the agricultural expansion in the region.",
